[{:db/id "q-38467/selection/7d00f9b66830b14fefc14bf7531dbbd2d05f295ddd76a38bfd102c324772b0e1" :answer/id #uuid "f815fe24-38e4-587d-8bb9-6e02340f19eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38467/selection/76c690f03fbd5162fa21765f31a2046fdb1ba896a35e9b165f53f25a86cd1745" :answer/id #uuid "9ce22d85-2d01-55a1-8f42-3d90331eea0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38467/selection/044625205d52a58e07f5170ef6374e33e6ab6ff0d1713191766e66f1bf74dad9" :answer/id #uuid "2235728e-c5ec-5a68-a736-d44dee40dccf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38467/selection/785f053bcefb11036ea74abd04112aaa84b17a5de4012606fb127a671f363cff" :answer/id #uuid "663493ee-5b7c-5e85-a237-b56c970fc081" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38467/selection/2b44e6d43e3927389e0c1c2c163b7136f70bbb82b73accf5d4c97d2f0dd2b207" :answer/id #uuid "7dae2341-8f36-51ba-8659-c02ac387f453" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38467/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3421e055-f498-5dc0-b76b-ec8c1d039b20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38467/selection/044625205d52a58e07f5170ef6374e33e6ab6ff0d1713191766e66f1bf74dad9" :answer-field/choices ["q-38467/selection/7d00f9b66830b14fefc14bf7531dbbd2d05f295ddd76a38bfd102c324772b0e1" "q-38467/selection/76c690f03fbd5162fa21765f31a2046fdb1ba896a35e9b165f53f25a86cd1745" "q-38467/selection/044625205d52a58e07f5170ef6374e33e6ab6ff0d1713191766e66f1bf74dad9" "q-38467/selection/785f053bcefb11036ea74abd04112aaa84b17a5de4012606fb127a671f363cff" "q-38467/selection/2b44e6d43e3927389e0c1c2c163b7136f70bbb82b73accf5d4c97d2f0dd2b207"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38467" :question/id #uuid "fac565dd-9d2a-5baf-a321-5d551f31320f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38467" :question/problem "Change the order of integration and evaluate the following double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/a85f82756c621bf88b95451f54343be863345278f361fd0f0dd82f5d01c0cb5b.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/8243a8c60e4b8b4846d330a00a090d6f93f94f17323c1d0a88d486ba77745451.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{[\\frac{2}{6}\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\sqrt{2{y}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}-1)}{2}[{y}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-38467/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1723a1-c676-517c-8dc5-f2b61ba017c6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38467"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82350/selection/afe32cd6e2fa10e34acc689e8452369bb9c0b5d991817763a9643fa4c16ea30c" :answer/id #uuid "cf4ed644-724e-58ae-9ed2-8db417779a4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{(y+2)/2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82350/selection/3152415f3e94c573f3e850551c732e9c6f2f7390a17c07a8a627440706747e71" :answer/id #uuid "3a4aa1b4-6145-5c72-ac78-9676131ea005" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{(y+2)/2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82350/selection/92b359af2a7759f6a8d9983accc00554e508067d90b282718bc794554abce107" :answer/id #uuid "9ec8b628-11b5-5c33-811e-c871b8cbe10f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}^{(y+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82350/selection/07f9cd4046c0edfefbfac2d4780a853da4da9a4b1906fbf69b2f86f184492717" :answer/id #uuid "f383d194-0500-56f6-94ac-daf1374bc8c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{(y+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82350/selection/a09c5857573cd71af53f2dde02c793cf7f4ba0fa8a9264f09f6cc88dec781d95" :answer/id #uuid "ebbbc741-8442-5657-952b-60cc8ea76a0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{(y+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82350/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7472e21a-1a1e-56d1-93bf-2a6ade1fdc35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82350/selection/07f9cd4046c0edfefbfac2d4780a853da4da9a4b1906fbf69b2f86f184492717" :answer-field/choices ["q-82350/selection/afe32cd6e2fa10e34acc689e8452369bb9c0b5d991817763a9643fa4c16ea30c" "q-82350/selection/3152415f3e94c573f3e850551c732e9c6f2f7390a17c07a8a627440706747e71" "q-82350/selection/92b359af2a7759f6a8d9983accc00554e508067d90b282718bc794554abce107" "q-82350/selection/07f9cd4046c0edfefbfac2d4780a853da4da9a4b1906fbf69b2f86f184492717" "q-82350/selection/a09c5857573cd71af53f2dde02c793cf7f4ba0fa8a9264f09f6cc88dec781d95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82350" :question/id #uuid "14bb10d0-476b-5119-9373-9c2a75131b52" :question/math-academy-id "q-82350" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2x-2}^{1-{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/0119869a8627edfaf9c16f905908d378b94c9566b0a6b7742c813c35f58d4699.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2x-2\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/3fe0d83ae8f99f443646be4e84687104edaeef58a83e68da7e832630f31efda7.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$\\,$ $x=\\frac{y+2}{2}.$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt[3]{1-y}.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{y+2}{2}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{1-y}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2x-2}^{1-{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{(y+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-82350/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82350"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132564/selection/236529adc5a010177978ad60ac949c6d00177723cbbe81734fb24fb4a68c0ce8" :answer/id #uuid "a472365b-1320-549d-88c1-1eed95f02f54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{-x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132564/selection/a15b5b662f475658e342790328c0e868baf2ac5daf84394e3b7e6386ba59a290" :answer/id #uuid "5c322761-a41e-5219-94f7-d094f9a7b120" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{-x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132564/selection/d1058cecea5258031879d26e8f40516a4517eeed8225120b5608b775305c206d" :answer/id #uuid "752ecec7-4018-5026-9670-8f938579b26b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132564/selection/803150ff77a45075db5ef11a862f1f0bb2f12c4c3b617bef212775957aae9138" :answer/id #uuid "30274e62-55a6-558f-967d-ad936d4182a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132564/selection/12f733476c097bf6837375027d14a2afd54c6b5fbcc2292bd3c4e1b07960fdcd" :answer/id #uuid "1ffc4046-2f5a-5ea3-a3d8-1b89a03601d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132564/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0e30dbf-282e-5394-80bd-7e1e28c8fbbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132564/selection/d1058cecea5258031879d26e8f40516a4517eeed8225120b5608b775305c206d" :answer-field/choices ["q-132564/selection/236529adc5a010177978ad60ac949c6d00177723cbbe81734fb24fb4a68c0ce8" "q-132564/selection/a15b5b662f475658e342790328c0e868baf2ac5daf84394e3b7e6386ba59a290" "q-132564/selection/d1058cecea5258031879d26e8f40516a4517eeed8225120b5608b775305c206d" "q-132564/selection/803150ff77a45075db5ef11a862f1f0bb2f12c4c3b617bef212775957aae9138" "q-132564/selection/12f733476c097bf6837375027d14a2afd54c6b5fbcc2292bd3c4e1b07960fdcd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132564" :question/id #uuid "fac1e7c0-0a06-5b8c-ba15-80235cdce89f" :question/math-academy-id "q-132564" :question/problem "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\n$$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/9a539f69187276895f8f53e2107c1959fefd0aeb7126dcff049569bfc8bc49d3.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type II regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y-2\\le x\\le 0}\\,\\cup \\,{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y-2\\le x\\le 0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=y-2\\,⟹\\,y=x+2,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=-y-2\\,⟹\\,y=-x-2.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x-2\\le y\\le x+2},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/ba9c9132c8efdb811e63bebc05e1f46bc8cbc54bcb8246072013a75d53bcb4df.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132564/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132564"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132574/selection/2726626922428acb497deb7604c920bd3df7f02a6c8c6c0b54b41feba976b467" :answer/id #uuid "5db22132-5481-553d-941b-41c0cf7e6aa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132574/selection/078f3608c30bf25780c005bf3e44a53bfaaff8bb837556a039245384567692af" :answer/id #uuid "c32ef605-63f0-51b9-ac59-7e3f5a12d115" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132574/selection/f01b2ffb5c222cfb3d4430c8e8bb034ca61cf76bf8c7ac55f77adeb26d08dba6" :answer/id #uuid "46cb823a-2d89-588f-87dd-164c5c3bc273" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132574/selection/9865bb50258298517480766a0dc8127740e307a19fe1f7d8d799a435f5ccddf4" :answer/id #uuid "995f51e1-5066-5228-b5fb-5ae8f28a7044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132574/selection/b324f321f3e17bc2ab58e1e69dc2184e373522d04002d28efa14b75c34eec42b" :answer/id #uuid "009123d0-6af3-5634-af29-337b8b207606" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132574/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8f9c0dc-1aaf-5421-b9f9-2c3369441a75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132574/selection/078f3608c30bf25780c005bf3e44a53bfaaff8bb837556a039245384567692af" :answer-field/choices ["q-132574/selection/2726626922428acb497deb7604c920bd3df7f02a6c8c6c0b54b41feba976b467" "q-132574/selection/078f3608c30bf25780c005bf3e44a53bfaaff8bb837556a039245384567692af" "q-132574/selection/f01b2ffb5c222cfb3d4430c8e8bb034ca61cf76bf8c7ac55f77adeb26d08dba6" "q-132574/selection/9865bb50258298517480766a0dc8127740e307a19fe1f7d8d799a435f5ccddf4" "q-132574/selection/b324f321f3e17bc2ab58e1e69dc2184e373522d04002d28efa14b75c34eec42b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132574" :question/id #uuid "beadb269-b7ea-53ff-b4f5-7e076bd62818" :question/math-academy-id "q-132574" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}-1}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/926e4c717707d13fdb9562e149d2f41c3ab657b42fbae35c0953019ab93a06b6.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-{y}^{2}-1\\le x\\le -y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/8933233e8aca4a36ee90ffec69ca6e93d0523d3fa50c400d2cdea78f9ec80812.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $y=y(x),$  are \n\n$\\,$ $y=\\sqrt{-x-1}\\,$ and $\\,y=1.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=-x.$ \n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le -1,\\,\\sqrt{-x-1}\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le -x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}-1}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132574/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132574"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132635/selection/eb1b3531ea2be21db34cdbfb6e8ce2849cec7b2e87145fc991070e440f403bbd" :answer/id #uuid "d914912a-2d24-5597-b221-453c818503f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132635/selection/5f766fb36b2e5b7453762eac481b87d70d75b5581540fc74a6673361b91f9598" :answer/id #uuid "928b392f-e22a-53e9-b267-2b4c7560b41a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3-1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132635/selection/3189eb800cec7c127da5feb1121556edf105eb4a44935fdef66273ee861e4406" :answer/id #uuid "5f0eaf24-9fd3-5e97-bfaa-182789ed186b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132635/selection/fd772afca031f4643a7586d517b4465d0c4659a743c6882b728b7fee8ff14a8e" :answer/id #uuid "30a58be5-ed69-5441-8e7b-671463340262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡3-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132635/selection/bbe600c473320d00dc1a27c826cbda963b9bcd268c2687e5f28d3d23baf215e5" :answer/id #uuid "2e6bedbb-601c-573a-ae08-f3048901e4f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132635/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "515d3dea-5d71-54fe-8f97-6c1dd96b6965" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132635/selection/5f766fb36b2e5b7453762eac481b87d70d75b5581540fc74a6673361b91f9598" :answer-field/choices ["q-132635/selection/eb1b3531ea2be21db34cdbfb6e8ce2849cec7b2e87145fc991070e440f403bbd" "q-132635/selection/5f766fb36b2e5b7453762eac481b87d70d75b5581540fc74a6673361b91f9598" "q-132635/selection/3189eb800cec7c127da5feb1121556edf105eb4a44935fdef66273ee861e4406" "q-132635/selection/fd772afca031f4643a7586d517b4465d0c4659a743c6882b728b7fee8ff14a8e" "q-132635/selection/bbe600c473320d00dc1a27c826cbda963b9bcd268c2687e5f28d3d23baf215e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132635" :question/id #uuid "7366d4ed-861b-5bc3-8ff6-f75a3451a58f" :question/math-academy-id "q-132635" :question/problem "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/8ed09966d887f66f36402df0047ba02444d92b8aa4c3cb744721bb4ad6278812.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,\\sqrt[3]{y}\\le x\\le 0}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt[3]{y}\\,⟹\\,y={x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=-1.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,-1\\le y\\le {x}^{3}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14079520/assets/f707a71f68f2e030696029d9a919e16ae6afda18a1d60dc3f8113f03143243e7.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{{x}^{3}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)[{\\int }_{-1}^{{x}^{3}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\cdot y\\,{|}_{-1}^{{x}^{3}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({x}^{3}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{4}+4x)\\,{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({0}^{4}+4(0))-(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡((-1)^{4}+4(-1))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡3-1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132635/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1723a1-c676-517c-8dc5-f2b61ba017c6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132635"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
